"Basal metabolic rate (BMR) refers to the minimum energy expenditure required for the human body to maintain life at rest. The Mifflin-St. Jeor formula is typically used:

Men's BMR = 10 × weight (kg) + 6.25 × height (cm) - 5 × age + 5;
Women's BMR = 10 × weight (kg) + 6.25 × height (cm) - 5 × age - 161;

In practical applications, it's necessary to combine activity coefficients (e.g., sedentary 1.2, moderate-intensity exercise 1.55, etc.) to estimate total daily energy expenditure."
